A.q3=s(["These are the numbers you remember quoting, not a recording of what you said. Treat the gap as a rough size, not an exact one.","The gap is measured only on jobs you won, because only those have a bill. Quotes you lost are counted, but they carry no gap. So this sheet cannot see the jobs you lost because the quote was too high. Read the gap column and the acceptance column together: a job type you win almost every time may simply be quoted low.",'Walked-away jobs are counted in their own column, and the acceptance rate is printed twice \u2014 once over decided quotes (won + lost) and once over every quote you gave (won + lost + walked away). "Never came back" is more often a soft no than a neutral event, so both denominators are shown. Where more customers walked away than ever decided, no single percentage is printed at all: the raw counts are printed instead.',"Jobs you quoted at zero \u2014 free or warranty work \u2014 are left out of BOTH gap figures and counted separately on the row. A job that was never quoted cannot measure how you quote.","Every figure shows how many jobs it came from. Where there are too few, the cell is blank \u2014 takhmeena would rather print nothing than print a number you would act on. The two minimums cannot be set below 3.",'The "All job types" row carries counts and money totals only. A gap or a rate pooled across different kinds of work measures the job mix, not the quoting.',"takhmeena has no price list, knows nothing about your costs, and makes no recommendation. It reports two numbers you entered and the distance between them.","Your data is a SQLite file on your machine. The app runs on localhost. There is no account, no sync, no encryption, and nothing is uploaded anywhere."],t.s)
